Thus it goes like this:

$ pip install virtualenv --break-system-packages

If this error appears:

WARNING: The script virtualenv is installed in '/home/xy/.local/bin' which is not on PATH.

Add to the path with the following commands:

$ echo 'export PATH="$PATH:/home/xy/.local/bin"' >> ~/.bashrc
$ source ~/.bashrc

Then create a virtualenv:

$ virtualenv *any_name_you_like_to_use*

Enter the virtualenv:

$ source *any_name_you_like_to_use*

Then:

$ pip install matplotlib pandas numpy scikit-learn seaborn jupyterlab

Then from the site:
https://docs.rapids.ai/install/#system-req

The code should be if you keep it minimal. It varies of course. 

pip install \
    "cudf-cu13==26.6.*" "cuml-cu13==26.6.*"

Torch from here:
https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/

The code should be like this:
$ pip3 install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu132

It should be in working condition now. I couldn't use the latest cuml packages on the Ubuntu 22.04 so I had install the 26.04 to have the latest for now. 
Enjoy! 
